{{ config(model_type="agent", agent_step_limit=80, agent_cost_limit=1) }}
Collect evidence for someone writing an OrcaSlicer 2.5 plugin that, after slicing a
Bambu Lab A1 job, replaces the end G-code and repeats the print N times. They will
only trust what you quote, so quote; do not summarise from memory.

Tools (bash; `$BRAVE_API_KEY` is set; Brave allows 1 request/second, so `sleep 1.1` between searches):
- Search: `curl -s -G https://api.search.brave.com/res/v1/web/search --data-urlencode "q=QUERY" -H "X-Subscription-Token: $BRAVE_API_KEY" -H "Accept: application/json"` -> `.web.results[].url/.description`
- Fetch, in order, moving on only if the previous one fails or returns under ~1500 chars of page text:
  1. `curl -sL URL` (most wiki pages are plain HTML; the article is inside `<main>`)
  2. headless Playwright: `PW_CORE=$(dirname $(node -e "console.log(require.resolve('playwright-core/package.json',{paths:['$(npm root -g)/@playwright/mcp']}))"))`, then a node script doing `require(process.env.PW_CORE).chromium.launch({channel:"chrome",headless:true})`, `page.goto(URL,{waitUntil:"networkidle"})`, print `page.content()`
  3. Chrome from bash: `"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome" --headless=new --disable-gpu --virtual-time-budget=8000 --dump-dom URL`
  Strip tags to text (python3 is available) and read the `<main>` part.

Steps:
1. Search for the OrcaSlicer plugin system, plugin development, plugin API reference
   (registry, slicing pipeline, host, host UI, script) and the 2.5.0 alpha release notes.
   Prefer orcaslicer.com/wiki and github.com/OrcaSlicer.
2. Fetch and read each relevant page (start with these, then follow links that matter):
   https://www.orcaslicer.com/wiki/developer_reference/plugin_development/plugin_system
   https://www.orcaslicer.com/wiki/developer_reference/plugin_development/plugin_development
   https://www.orcaslicer.com/wiki/developer_reference/plugin_development/api_reference/slicing
   https://www.orcaslicer.com/wiki/developer_reference/plugin_development/api_reference/registry
3. Record verbatim excerpts covering: plugin types, the manifest / PEP 723
   `[tool.orcaslicer.plugin]` fields, every hook or callback with its exact signature,
   how a plugin gets user parameters, how it loads dependencies, sandbox prompts, and
   anything about reading or modifying G-code after slicing.
4. If a page will not load by any of the three methods, or a topic is covered nowhere,
   write MISSING for it.

Deliver the answer as your final submitted message, not as a file: do not write to
`outputs/` (an earlier run saved answer.txt there and the next step saw only its hash).
Answer in this format only (one block per page, then the gaps):

SOURCES:
- <url> (fetched with: curl | playwright | chrome)
EXCERPTS:
> <verbatim text>

MISSING:
- <topic>: <where you looked>
